#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/index.md:1
msgid "fit_utils.py"
msgstr "fit_utils.py"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/index.md:3
msgid ""
"`fit_utils.py` implements MesPy's linear fitting function and its immutable "
"result object."
msgstr ""
"`fit_utils.py` implements MesPy's linear fitting function and its immutable "
"result object."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/index.md:5
msgid "Public interface"
msgstr "Public interface"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/index.md:7
msgid ""
"[`lin_fit`](lin-fit.md): OLS, absolute WLS, and optional horizontal "
"uncertainty propagation selected explicitly through `x_error_method`."
msgstr ""
"[`lin_fit`](lin-fit.md): OLS, absolute WLS, and optional horizontal "
"uncertainty propagation selected explicitly through `x_error_method`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/index.md:8
msgid ""
"[`LinearFitResult`](linear-fit-result.md): fitted parameters, uncertainties,"
" physical residuals, diagnostics, prediction, and TOML export."
msgstr ""
"[`LinearFitResult`](linear-fit-result.md): fitted parameters, uncertainties,"
" physical residuals, diagnostics, prediction, and TOML export."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/index.md:9
msgid ""
"`XErrorMethod`: the type alias `Literal[\"none\", \"iterate\"]` for "
"horizontal uncertainty treatment."
msgstr ""
"`XErrorMethod`: the type alias `Literal[\"none\", \"iterate\"]` for "
"horizontal uncertainty treatment."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/index.md:11
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr "Implementation"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/index.md:13
msgid ""
"The module validates finite real input vectors, positive vertical "
"uncertainties, and optional non-negative horizontal uncertainties. Centered "
"and scaled coordinates preserve numerical accuracy for fitting and "
"prediction. Optional effective-variance iteration has fixed convergence "
"settings; `fit_method`, `tol`, and `max_iter` are no longer public input "
"arguments."
msgstr ""
"The module validates finite real input vectors, positive vertical "
"uncertainties, and optional non-negative horizontal uncertainties. Centered "
"and scaled coordinates preserve numerical accuracy for fitting and "
"prediction. Optional effective-variance iteration has fixed convergence "
"settings; `fit_method`, `tol`, and `max_iter` are no longer public input "
"arguments."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/index.md:15
msgid ""
"Plotting uses the shared [style context](../../checks/plot_utils/style-"
"context.md), with `\"mespy\"` as the default style. Export writes TOML and, "
"when plotting is enabled, PDF files from an extension-free base path. The "
"[function reference](lin-fit.md) describes validation, iteration, plotting, "
"and export in detail."
msgstr ""
"Plotting uses the shared [style context](../../checks/plot_utils/style-"
"context.md), with `\"mespy\"` as the default style. Export writes TOML and, "
"when plotting is enabled, PDF files from an extension-free base path. The "
"[function reference](lin-fit.md) describes validation, iteration, plotting, "
"and export in detail."
